<section class="section" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="section__head">
    <div>
      <h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p>Quick answers about this mirror directory.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="faq">
    <details open>
      <summary>Is GKStreams down right now?</summary>
      <p>
        This page only lists mirrors that are <strong>currently online</strong>. If you see
        cards above, those domains passed our last check (every 5 minutes). If the list is
        empty, all mirrors were down at the last check — refresh in a few minutes.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>What is a GKStreams mirror?</summary>
      <p>
        A mirror is an alternate address for the same service. This landing page only
        <strong>lists</strong> addresses that are up. It does not host streams, embed
        players, or store any media.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>How often is status updated?</summary>
      <p>
        Automated checks run every 5 minutes. Domains that go down are removed from this
        list until they recover.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Does this website host any streams?</summary>
      <p>
        No. This is an informational directory only — no video, audio, embed, or playback
        on this domain. Links go to third-party sites we do not control. See our
        <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer and DMCA policy</a>.
      </p>
    </details>

    <details>
      <summary>Why did a mirror disappear from the list?</summary>
      <p>
        If a domain fails the automated check, it is hidden until it is reachable again.
        That keeps this page limited to working mirrors only.
      </p>
    </details>
  </div>
</section>
